-- title:
--   Primes under the supersingular point lift to the Drinfeld chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$, and a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $q\ell$, together with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\xi \in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and $\zeta = \xi^{\ell}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subset L((t))$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the image, under coefficientwise base change along $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField` of level $(q^2M', H_1)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the base change of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157); let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $z$ be a point of $\mathfrak{X} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) at whose stalk the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ (taken through the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$) lies in the maximal ideal, and let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j)$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y) = z$ such that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $x$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $x$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Assume further a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with maximal ideal generated by $\sigma\varpi$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0, X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ at its maximal ideal onto $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma\varpi)v - fu)$ carrying, for every $a \in A$, the image of the germ of $a$ to the class of the constant series $C(\sigma a)$. Then for every prime ideal $\mathfrak{p}$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ containing the image of $\varpi$ and satisfying $\mathfrak{p} \le y$ and $\mathfrak{p} \neq y$, there is a prime ideal $P'$ of $S$ containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, with at least one of the classes of $X_0$, $X_1$ outside $P'$, whose contraction along the composite of the germ map $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j \to \mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ (through the open image of $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$), the completion map, and $e$ equals $\mathfrak{p}$.
--
--   This is the going-down step on the special fibre of the two-chart integral model: each prime of the $j$-finite chart strictly below the supersingular point $z$, containing the uniformiser, is the contraction of a prime of the Drinfeld-type formal chart $S$ that is not the maximal ideal, i.e. of a branch through the node. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.forall_mem_comap_drinfeldChart_iff_forall_coeff_mem_maximalIdeal_of_linearPart_riders_twoChartIntegralModel_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.forall_mem_comap_drinfeldChart_iff_forall_coeff_mem_maximalIdeal_of_linearPart_riders_twoChartIntegralModel_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd), in the auxiliary-level ($\Gamma_1(\ell)$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \bmod 12$) treatment allowing small $q$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevelOne_exists_isPrime_comap_drinfeldChart_eq_of_isPrime_le_ne_twoChartIntegralModel_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd.lean

